{"nodes":[{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup","label":"Visual Companion Final Hardening Fixup Implementation Plan","file_type":"document","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_rationale","label":"Goal: finish PR #1720 final hardening fixup with test-first changes, clean rebase state, reviewer-ready evidence","file_type":"rationale","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Keep the companion zero-dependency and local-first; add focused guards to the existing server and shell scripts (root screen containment, fallback token tracking, per-start instance id ownership proof) rather than new infrastructure."},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_root_screen_containment","label":"Root Screen Containment Guard","file_type":"concept","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Root screen selection could serve state/server-info through a symlink or hardlink inside the content dir; reusing the /files/* containment guard (isRegularFileInsideContentDir) closes the escape."},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_fallback_token_isolation","label":"Fallback Token Isolation","file_type":"concept","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A fallback server reusing the persisted token would let its key authenticate against the original server and could overwrite .last-token; tracking token source and rotating (or failing closed on explicit BRAINSTORM_TOKEN) isolates sessions."},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_instance_id_ownership","label":"Stop-Server Instance-Id Ownership Proof","file_type":"concept","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Command-name-only proof can kill impostor processes; a per-start command-line instance id (--brainstorm-server-id=<id>, stored in state/server-instance-id) gives stop-server exact ownership proof and fails closed on missing/mismatched/malformed ids."},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_fixed_port_guard","label":"Fixed-Port Test Guard and Skip-Aware Harness","file_type":"concept","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Fixed-port tests must not silently run through the EADDRINUSE port fallback; a guard asserting the expected port plus a SkipTest-aware harness keeps symlink/hardlink capability tests portable across hosts."},{"id":"docs_superpowers_plans_2026_06_11_visual_companion_final_hardening_fixup_pr_1720","label":"PR #1720 (brainstorming-companion final hardening fixup)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-11-visual-companion-final-hardening-fixup.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributo